# `{ ...base(1), name, resolved }` where the type that is written lists the names in another order: the keys of the object come in the order of what base() gives and then the names that the literal writes.
# The plan holds that order, so the object is born whole; without it the object is born with the one field that the declared order shares and the others are defined one by one through a stub.
# f1 = base, f2 = ref
